 "pages": "p.3 (ROC), p.5 (digital outputs, data format DB4), p.9-10 (pinout, terminal functions), p.11 (Figures 1-2), p.12 (timing: tCONV 3.2 us, tD6 60 ns at BVDD 3 V), p.20-21 (CLK, RESET, FD, EOC, HOLDx, reading data), p.22 (soft trigger, Tables 2-4), p.23-24 (nap/power-down, getting data, output code, Table 5)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs and the internal 2.5 V reference (REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V differential code (8000h straight binary after reset, 0000h with DB4 = 1)",
  "only HOLDA (pin) starts a conversion; HOLDB/HOLDC pins, simultaneous holds and the ignoring of further HOLD pulses until the conversion is done are not modeled; the soft-trigger bits start one conversion without a channel",
  "the six output registers, cycle mode (A2 A1 A0 = 110), FIFO mode (111, including the dummy read after reset) with their read sequencing, the ADD = 1 address/data-valid word (1000 0000 0000 DV A2 A1 A0), the empty-FIFO zero word and the FD output: every address returns the 0 V result",
  "BYTE = 1 (8-bit reads: low byte then high byte on successive RD pulses) is not modeled (stateful per-read sequencing)",
  "control register bits NAP, ADD and A2-A0 are stored but OR-ing with the NAP/ADD/A2-A0 pins is not modeled (reads use the address pins only); NAP mode and the NAP pin have no digital effect; the PD bit powers the model down/up; the control register is write-only on the part (no read-back exists)",
  "the conversion runs on the external CLK (16.5 clocks to the output latch, 20 clocks per conversion, fCLK max 5 MHz); the model uses the 3.2 us maximum conversion time; EOC is a half-clock low pulse (100 ns at 5 MHz); latch delays while a read is in progress are not modeled",
  "data-bus bits D15-D8 are don't-care in a write; bus float delay is not specified (tDf 0); power-down recovery time"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS8365 only (ADS8365IPAG/IPAGR); the ADS8364 is the earlier, separate datasheet",
